# Guide headings

Authoritative heading rules: `Paragon_Markdown_Style_Rules.md` §5.7 (numbered heading dots) and §5.6 (no bold in ATX headings).

## Repo reminder

On chapter pages whose H1 is numbered (`# N. Title`), every `##` heading **MUST** use `## N.M. Title` (full stop after the section id). Nested detail may use `## N.M.P. Title` or `###` as the page already does. Keep cross-links and anchors in sync when renumbering.

Exceptions (descriptive H2s allowed):

- `user-guide/Home.md` (landing / index)
- Runbooks and workflow docs that are not numbered chapters (for example `Admin-Dashboard-Runbook.md`, `Cursor-Docs-as-Code.md`, `Cursor-Docs-Changelog.md`)

If a short lead-in does not deserve a section number, do **not** use an H2. Use a bold lead-in or a paragraph under the H1 instead.

Punctuation: see `no-em-dashes-in-markdown` (no em dashes or en-dash substitutes in any `.md` file).
